From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: krane <chris@krane.dev>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 20:07:10 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] fix(bluetooth): trust devices paired with "Always connect"

Local fix (not a pctrade/end4-pC backport)
Problem: pair() alone leaves the device untrusted, so BlueZ asks the agent to authorize every profile connection and a NoInputNoOutput agent setup drops audio reconnects.
Port: local
Drop when: the pinned BluetoothDeviceItem.qml trusts devices it pairs.
---
 .../ii/sidebarRight/bluetoothDevices/BluetoothDeviceItem.qml  | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/dots/.config/quickshell/ii/modules/ii/sidebarRight/bluetoothDevices/BluetoothDeviceItem.qml b/dots/.config/quickshell/ii/modules/ii/sidebarRight/bluetoothDevices/BluetoothDeviceItem.qml
index 7292212d..5372f671 100644
--- a/dots/.config/quickshell/ii/modules/ii/sidebarRight/bluetoothDevices/BluetoothDeviceItem.qml
+++ b/dots/.config/quickshell/ii/modules/ii/sidebarRight/bluetoothDevices/BluetoothDeviceItem.qml
@@ -95,7 +95,11 @@ DialogListItem {
                     if (root.device?.paired) {
                         root.device?.forget();
                     } else {
+                        // ii registers no BlueZ agent, so a device paired here is Paired but
+                        // not Trusted, and every later profile connection needs the agent to
+                        // authorize it. Trust it too so reconnects don't need that agent.
                         root.device?.pair();
+                        root.device.trusted = true;
                     }
                 }
             }
